.TH CMEMPOOL_CREATE 3 "2026-10-30" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
cmempool_create \- create a fixed-size memory pool
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cmempool.h>

cmempool_create(elem_count, elem_size, fallback_to_dynamic_memory,
                single_threaded, err);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Creates a memory pool that manages a fixed number of elements of one
size. The pool's own memory and its fallback entries come from the
standard malloc and free.

It is the same as calling cmempool_create_mp() with NULL memory
management procedures, and every rule of that page applies: the
stride, the sizing advice and the thread safety.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
elem_count                 Number of elements in the pool (must be > 0)
elem_size                  Size of each element in bytes. It must be
                           > 0. The minimum is sizeof(uintptr_t). The
                           maximum is SIZE_MAX less the stride rounding
fallback_to_dynamic_memory If true, allocate from the heap when the pool
                           is empty
single_threaded            If true, take no lock (faster, but not
                           thread-safe)
err                        Optional pointer that receives an error string
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Returns a pointer to the new memory pool on success
Returns NULL on failure
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
The caller must destroy the pool with cmempool_destroy().
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cmempool_create_mp (3),
.BR cmempool_create_from_preallocated_buffer (3),
.BR cmempool_destroy (3)
